      },
      "text": "┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n         │                                                        │\n LENS →  │         ╱ mirror (raised for exposure)                 │\n         │  ┌───╱ mirror (down for viewing) ─────────► Pentaprism │\n         │  │                                                  │  │\n         │  ▼                                                  ▼  │\n         │ Focus screen (shows image projected by lens)  Eyepiece │\n         │                                                        │\n         └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                ↓ (at exposure)\n                          Film / Sensor plane"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:photography:05-camera-technology, git-history:photography:05-camera-technology]",
        "canonical_path": "photography/05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[camera, technology]",
        "current_path": "photography/05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:photography:camera-technology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "photography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[camera, technology]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Camera Technology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPERATION:\n  Viewing: mirror down → image refracted up by mirror → projected on focus screen\n           pentaprism (5-sided prism) corrects image: mirrors left-right twice\n           → correct-orientation image at eye\n  Exposure: press shutter → mirror flips up (blackout) → focal plane shutter opens\n            → sensor/film exposed → shutter closes → mirror returns"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:photography:05-camera-technology, git-history:photography:05-camera-technology]",
        "canonical_path": "photography/05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[camera, technology]",
        "current_path": "photography/05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:photography:camera-technology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "photography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[camera, technology]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Camera Technology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FOCAL PLANE SHUTTER:\n  Two curtains (blinds) that travel across the film/sensor plane\n  First curtain opens (travels from one side) → exposes sensor\n  Second curtain follows after delay = shutter speed\n  At fast speeds: second curtain chases first → only a slit exposes at any moment\n  X-sync (flash sync) speed: the slowest speed at which entire sensor is open simultaneously\n    → required for flash synchronization\n    Typical: 1/200s–1/250s for focal plane shutters\n    Above sync speed: slit = only part lit by flash → dark band in image"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-CAMERA-TECHNOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
